# Every text file checks out LF on every OS. Verification pins hashes over
# raw file bytes (exposure bundle chain, execution-map generation IDs,
# release authority modules, Cargo manifests), so a Windows CRLF checkout
# breaks them all the same way (proven twice on CI: hash-chain load failure,
# then authority + manifest drift on the very next run). No CRLF blobs exist
# in the index, so no fixture depends on checked-in CRLF bytes.
* text eol=lf
